---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="physics"
  title="Band Theory"
  description="One atom has levels. Bring a line of them close enough to notice each other and every level splits into as many as there are atoms, packed into a band. Which bands are full and how wide the gap is decides, on its own, whether you are holding a metal, a semiconductor or a rock."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="bt" class="bt-canvas" width="1000" height="880"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Pause</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Reset</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Atomic spacing a <b id="aval">2.50 Å</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="a" min="160" max="420" step="2" value="250" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>squeezed</span><span>far apart</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Electrons per atom <b id="nval">2</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="n" min="1" max="4" step="1" value="2" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>1</span><span>4</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Temperature <b id="tval">300 K</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="temp" min="10" max="1500" step="10" value="300" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Applied field <b id="fval">0.30</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="field" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="30" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>none</span><span>strong</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Time rate <b id="rateval">1.0×</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="rate" min="10" max="200" step="5" value="100" />
      </div>

      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="levels" checked /> Show the individual levels</label>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span id="l1">Verdict</span><b id="r1">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l2">Band gap</span><b id="r2">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l3">Lower band width</span><b id="r3">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l4">Fermi level</span><b id="r4">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l5">Free carriers</span><b id="r5">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l6">Drift velocity</span><b id="r6">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l7">Thermal energy kT</span><b id="r7">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        A chain of atoms with one s and one p level each, solved exactly by
        tight binding. Everything on screen comes out of that one model.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Start with the atoms far apart. Each band collapses to a single sharp
      level, the level an isolated atom has. Now bring them together. Every
      level <b>splits into as many levels as there are atoms</b>, because no two
      electrons may share a state, and the split widens the closer they get.
      That fan is where a band comes from.
    </li>
    <li>
      Watch the two fans as you squeeze. First they widen, then the gap between
      them narrows, and at close enough spacing they <b>overlap and the gap is
      gone</b>. Nothing about the atoms changed. Being an insulator or a metal
      can be a matter of how far apart you hold the same atoms.
    </li>
    <li>
      Set two electrons per atom and look at the occupied states: the lower band
      is exactly full. Now turn the field up. The whole sea of occupied states
      tries to shift, and <b>nothing happens</b>, because a full band shifted is
      still a full band. For every electron moving one way there is one moving
      the other. That is what an insulator is, and it is a counting argument,
      not a strength argument.
    </li>
    <li>
      Change to one electron per atom. The same band is now half full, there is
      a Fermi surface, and the sea can lean sideways. Watch the drift velocity
      jump and the electrons in the crystal start moving. Odd electrons per atom
      and you have a metal, almost for free.
    </li>
    <li>
      Go back to two per atom and set a spacing where the gap is about one
      electron volt. Now raise the temperature. A few electrons make it across
      the gap, leaving holes behind, and the conduction climbs steeply because
      the number of carriers goes as e<sup>−E<sub>g</sub>/2kT</sup>. This is a
      semiconductor, and this is why heating one makes it conduct better while
      heating a metal makes it worse.
    </li>
    <li>
      Compare kT against the gap in the readout. At room temperature kT is about
      0.026 eV, so a 5 eV gap is untouchable and a 1 eV gap is merely very
      unlikely. The whole difference between a diamond and a chip is that ratio.
    </li>
    <li>
      Look at the density of states. It piles up at the band edges and thins in
      the middle, and the Fermi-Dirac curve beside it is a soft step whose
      softness is a few kT wide. The states are what the crystal offers, the
      curve is what temperature takes up, and everything electrical is the
      product of the two.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText, subHtml } from '../../../lib/sim';
  import { equationBar } from '../../../lib/equation';

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // A one dimensional chain with one s and one p orbital per atom, nearest
  // neighbour tight binding. Two bands, one gap, and every number on screen
  // comes from these few lines.
  //   E_s(θ) = Es − 2 t_s cos θ      E_p(θ) = Ep + 2 t_p cos θ,  θ = k·a
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  const ES = -8.0, EP = -2.5; // isolated atom levels, eV
  const KB = 8.617333e-5; // eV/K
  const NK = 220; // k points across the Brillouin zone

  const state = {
    a: 2.5, // atomic spacing, Å
    n: 2, // electrons per atom
    temp: 300,
    field: 0.3,
    rate: 1,
    running: true,
    levels: true,
  };

  /** Overlap falls off exponentially with distance: that is the whole story. */
  const tS = (a = state.a) => 28.4 * Math.exp(-a / 0.7);
  const tP = (a = state.a) => 1.7 * tS(a);
  const band1 = (th: number, a = state.a) => ES - 2 * tS(a) * Math.cos(th);
  const band2 = (th: number, a = state.a) => EP + 2 * tP(a) * Math.cos(th);
  const gap = (a = state.a) => EP - 2 * tP(a) - (ES + 2 * tS(a));
  const kT = () => KB * state.temp;

  /** dE/dk turned into a real velocity, in m/s. */
  const vel1 = (th: number) => state.a * 2 * tS() * Math.sin(th) * 1.519e5;
  const vel2 = (th: number) => -state.a * 2 * tP() * Math.sin(th) * 1.519e5;

  const fermi = (E: number, EF: number) => 1 / (1 + Math.exp(Math.min(60, (E - EF) / kT())));

  const thetas: number[] = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < NK; i++) thetas.push(-Math.PI + ((i + 0.5) * 2 * Math.PI) / NK);

  /** Electrons per atom held at this Fermi level, both bands, both spins. */
  function countAt(EF: number) {
    let s = 0;
    for (const th of thetas) s += fermi(band1(th), EF) + fermi(band2(th), EF);
    return (2 * s) / NK;
  }

  const bandTop = () => Math.max(ES + 2 * tS(), EP + 2 * tP());

  /** log Σ exp(xᵢ) without overflowing, which is the whole difficulty here. */
  function logSumExp(xs: number[]) {
    const m = Math.max(...xs);
    let s = 0;
    for (const x of xs) s += Math.exp(x - m);
    return m + Math.log(s);
  }

  /**
   * Where the Fermi level sits when it lands in a gap. Counting electrons
   * cannot find it: across a wide gap every level in the gap holds exactly the
   * same number of electrons to within rounding, so a bisection on the count
   * stops wherever it first loses resolution and reports a Fermi level jammed
   * against the valence band. Balancing electrons against holes in logs is
   * well conditioned no matter how wide the gap gets.
   *   Σ e^(Ev/kT) · e^(−EF/kT) = Σ e^(−Ec/kT) · e^(EF/kT)
   */
  function intrinsicLevel(
    vb: (t: number) => number,
    cb: (t: number) => number
  ) {
    const kt = kT();
    const lv = logSumExp(thetas.map((t) => vb(t) / kt));
    const lc = logSumExp(thetas.map((t) => -cb(t) / kt));
    return 0.5 * kt * (lv - lc);
  }

  function fermiLevel() {
    // Every band full: the level belongs in the gap up to the next band, which
    // this two band model does not have.
    if (state.n >= 4) return bandTop() + 0.4;
    let lo = -20, hi = 6;
    for (let i = 0; i < 60; i++) {
      const m = 0.5 * (lo + hi);
      if (countAt(m) < state.n) lo = m;
      else hi = m;
    }
    const bis = 0.5 * (lo + hi);
    if (inBandAt(bis) || state.n !== 2) return bis;
    return intrinsicLevel(band1, band2);
  }

  /** Is there anything to sit in at this energy? That is the whole test. */
  function inBandAt(e: number) {
    const m = 1e-3;
    return (
      (e > ES - 2 * tS() + m && e < ES + 2 * tS() - m) ||
      (e > EP - 2 * tP() + m && e < EP + 2 * tP() - m)
    );
  }

  // Live quantities, recomputed once a frame.
  let EF = -6;
  let shift = 0; // how far the occupied sea has leaned, in θ
  let vDrift = 0; // m/s, averaged over every occupied state
  let carriers = 0; // fraction of states that are neither full nor empty
  let occ1: number[] = [], occ2: number[] = [];
  let fill1 = 0, fill2 = 0; // mean occupancy of each band

  function recompute() {
    EF = fermiLevel();
    occ1 = thetas.map((th) => fermi(band1(th - shift), EF));
    occ2 = thetas.map((th) => fermi(band2(th - shift), EF));
    let sum = 0, free = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < NK; i++) {
      sum += occ1[i] * vel1(thetas[i]) + occ2[i] * vel2(thetas[i]);
      // A state only carries current if it is neither certainly full nor
      // certainly empty, which is exactly 4f(1−f).
      const f1 = fermi(band1(thetas[i]), EF), f2 = fermi(band2(thetas[i]), EF);
      free += 4 * f1 * (1 - f1) + 4 * f2 * (1 - f2);
    }
    vDrift = (2 * sum) / (state.n * NK);
    carriers = free / (2 * NK);
    fill1 = occ1.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / NK;
    fill2 = occ2.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / NK;
  }

  function verdict() {
    // A metal is a crystal with states at the Fermi level. Counting thermally
    // active carriers cannot tell a cold metal from an insulator, because a
    // cold metal has few of those either.
    if (inBandAt(EF)) return gap() <= 0.02 ? 'metal (bands overlap)' : 'metal (partly filled band)';
    if (state.n >= 4) return 'insulator (every band full)';
    if (carriers > 1e-18) return 'semiconductor';
    return 'insulator';
  }

  // --- canvas ----------------------------------------------------------------

  const canvas = document.getElementById('bt') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const cssVar = (n: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
  const inkRGB = () => cssVar('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236';
  const inkA = (a: number) => `rgba(${inkRGB()},${a})`;
  const { label, textWidth } = makeText(ctx, inkA);

  const LOWER = '#f9736a'; // the lower band and its electrons
  const UPPER = '#5b8cff'; // the upper band
  const ACC = '#7c8cff';
  const WARM = '#f59e0b';
  const GREEN = '#34d399';

  const SPLIT = { x: 20, y: 88, w: 468, h: 322 };
  const CRYS = { x: 512, y: 88, w: 468, h: 322 };
  const BANDS = { x: 20, y: 462, w: 468, h: 378 };
  const OCC = { x: 512, y: 462, w: 468, h: 378 };

  function rr(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, r: number) {
    const rad = Math.min(r, Math.abs(w) / 2, Math.abs(h) / 2);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x + rad, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w - rad, y);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y, x + w, y + rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w, y + h - rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y + h, x + w - rad, y + h);
    ctx.lineTo(x + rad, y + h);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y + h, x, y + h - rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x, y + rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y, x + rad, y);
    ctx.closePath();
  }
  function panel(p: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number }, title: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.1);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    rr(p.x, p.y, p.w, p.h, 10);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(title, p.x + 2, p.y - 9, 0.5, 'left', 11);
  }
  function arrow(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number, size = 5) {
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x1, y1);
    ctx.lineTo(x2, y2);
    ctx.stroke();
    const an = Math.atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x2, y2);
    ctx.lineTo(x2 - size * Math.cos(an - 0.4), y2 - size * Math.sin(an - 0.4));
    ctx.lineTo(x2 - size * Math.cos(an + 0.4), y2 - size * Math.sin(an + 0.4));
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fill();
  }

  // --- where bands come from -------------------------------------------------

  const A_MIN = 1.6, A_MAX = 4.2;

  function drawSplit() {
    panel(SPLIT, 'WHERE A BAND COMES FROM');
    const px = SPLIT.x + 46, py = SPLIT.y + 26, pw = SPLIT.w - 66, ph = SPLIT.h - 74;
    // energy range wide enough for the widest fan the sliders can reach
    const eLo = ES - 2 * tS(A_MIN) - 0.6, eHi = EP + 2 * tP(A_MIN) + 0.6;
    const X = (a: number) => px + ((A_MAX - a) / (A_MAX - A_MIN)) * pw;
    const Y = (e: number) => py + ph - ((e - eLo) / (eHi - eLo)) * ph;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.2);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();

    // the two fans: each band's top and bottom edge against spacing
    const fills: [(th: number, a: number) => number, string, number][] = [
      [band1, LOWER, 0.16],
      [band2, UPPER, 0.16],
    ];
    for (const [fn, col, alpha] of fills) {
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let i = 0; i <= 80; i++) {
        const a = A_MAX - ((A_MAX - A_MIN) * i) / 80;
        const e = Math.max(fn(0, a), fn(Math.PI, a));
        i ? ctx.lineTo(X(a), Y(e)) : ctx.moveTo(X(a), Y(e));
      }
      for (let i = 80; i >= 0; i--) {
        const a = A_MAX - ((A_MAX - A_MIN) * i) / 80;
        const e = Math.min(fn(0, a), fn(Math.PI, a));
        ctx.lineTo(X(a), Y(e));
      }
      ctx.closePath();
      ctx.fillStyle = col.replace('#', 'rgba(').length ? col : col;
      ctx.globalAlpha = alpha;
      ctx.fillStyle = col;
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      ctx.strokeStyle = col;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    // the current spacing, and the discrete levels a short chain really has
    const xa = X(state.a);
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.45);
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(xa, py);
    ctx.lineTo(xa, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    if (state.levels) {
      const N = 8;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;
      for (let m = 1; m <= N; m++) {
        const c = Math.cos((m * Math.PI) / (N + 1));
        for (const [e, col] of [
          [ES - 2 * tS() * c, LOWER],
          [EP + 2 * tP() * c, UPPER],
        ] as [number, string][]) {
          ctx.strokeStyle = col;
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.moveTo(xa - 13, Y(e));
          ctx.lineTo(xa + 13, Y(e));
          ctx.stroke();
        }
      }
      const flip = xa > px + pw * 0.62;
      label('8 atoms, 8 levels', xa + (flip ? -18 : 18), py + 14, 0.45, flip ? 'right' : 'left', 10);
    }

    if (gap() > 0.02) {
      const yTop = Y(EP - 2 * tP()), yBot = Y(ES + 2 * tS());
      ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(245,158,11,0.08)';
      ctx.fillRect(px, yTop, pw, yBot - yTop);
      label('forbidden', px + pw - 6, (yTop + yBot) / 2 + 4, 0.45, 'right', 10, WARM);
    }

    label('the isolated atom', px + 4, Y(ES) - 9, 0.4, 'left', 10);
    label('energy (eV)', px + 4, py - 9, 0.4, 'left', 10);
    label(`${eHi.toFixed(0)}`, px - 6, py + 5, 0.35, 'right', 9);
    label(`${eLo.toFixed(0)}`, px - 6, py + ph, 0.35, 'right', 9);
    label('atoms far apart', px + 2, py + ph + 18, 0.4, 'left', 10);
    label('squeezed together', px + pw, py + ph + 18, 0.4, 'right', 10);
    label(`a = ${state.a.toFixed(2)} Å`, xa, py + ph + 34, 0.7, 'center', 11, ACC);
  }

  // --- the crystal itself ----------------------------------------------------

  type Mover = { x: number; y: number; band: number; ph: number };
  let movers: Mover[] = [];
  type Jump = { x: number; y0: number; y1: number; life: number };
  let jumps: Jump[] = [];

  function buildMovers() {
    recompute();
    movers = [];
    const total = 26;
    // Share the electrons out the way the occupancies actually do.
    const up = Math.round((total * fill2) / Math.max(1e-9, fill1 + fill2));
    for (let i = 0; i < total; i++)
      movers.push({
        x: Math.random(),
        y: Math.random(),
        band: i < up ? 1 : 0,
        ph: Math.random() * 6.3,
      });
  }

  function crystalGeom() {
    const y0 = CRYS.y + 108; // upper band lane
    const y1 = CRYS.y + 220; // lower band lane
    return { x0: CRYS.x + 34, x1: CRYS.x + CRYS.w - 34, y0, y1 };
  }

  function stepCrystal(dt: number) {
    const g = crystalGeom();
    const wpx = g.x1 - g.x0;
    // Electrons in the upper band ride the drift; those in the full lower band
    // are simply stuck, however hard you push.
    const vpx = Math.max(-260, Math.min(260, vDrift / 4000));
    for (const m of movers) {
      const stuck = (m.band === 1 ? fill2 : fill1) > 0.98;
      if (!stuck) {
        m.x += (vpx / wpx) * dt;
        m.x += ((Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.12) * dt;
        if (m.x > 1) m.x -= 1;
        if (m.x < 0) m.x += 1;
      } else {
        // a full band can still be pushed, it just cannot go anywhere
        m.x += ((Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.05) * dt;
        m.x = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, m.x));
      }
    }
    // thermal promotion across the gap, at the rate the statistics allow
    const rate = 60 * Math.exp(-Math.max(0, gap()) / (2 * kT()));
    if (Math.random() < rate * dt) {
      const cand = movers.filter((m) => m.band === 0);
      if (cand.length > 3) {
        const m = cand[(Math.random() * cand.length) | 0];
        m.band = 1;
        jumps.push({ x: g.x0 + m.x * wpx, y0: g.y1, y1: g.y0, life: 1 });
      }
    }
    // and the way back down
    if (Math.random() < 0.9 * dt) {
      const up = movers.filter((m) => m.band === 1);
      if (up.length > 0) {
        const m = up[(Math.random() * up.length) | 0];
        m.band = 0;
        jumps.push({ x: g.x0 + m.x * wpx, y0: g.y0, y1: g.y1, life: 1 });
      }
    }
    for (let k = jumps.length - 1; k >= 0; k--) {
      jumps[k].life -= dt * 2;
      if (jumps[k].life <= 0) jumps.splice(k, 1);
    }
  }

  function drawCrystal() {
    panel(CRYS, 'THE CRYSTAL, AND WHAT MOVES IN IT');
    const g = crystalGeom();
    const wpx = g.x1 - g.x0;
    const nAtoms = Math.max(4, Math.round(wpx / (state.a * 26)));

    // the potential: wells that overlap as the atoms come together
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.25);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;
    ctx.beginPath();
    const yBase = CRYS.y + 268;
    for (let i = 0; i <= 300; i++) {
      const x = g.x0 + (wpx * i) / 300;
      let v = 0;
      for (let k = 0; k < nAtoms; k++) {
        const xa = g.x0 + ((k + 0.5) * wpx) / nAtoms;
        const d = Math.abs(x - xa) / (wpx / nAtoms);
        v += 1 / (0.09 + d * d * 3.2);
      }
      const y = yBase - Math.min(58, v * 5.2);
      i ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y);
    }
    ctx.stroke();
    label('the potential the electrons sit in', g.x0, yBase + 22, 0.4, 'left', 10);

    // atoms
    for (let k = 0; k < nAtoms; k++) {
      const xa = g.x0 + ((k + 0.5) * wpx) / nAtoms;
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.4);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(xa, g.y1 + 44, 9, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    // the two lanes: a band each
    for (const [y, col, name] of [
      [g.y0, UPPER, 'upper band: room to move'],
      [g.y1, LOWER, 'lower band'],
    ] as [number, string, string][]) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = col;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.28;
      ctx.lineWidth = 16;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(g.x0, y);
      ctx.lineTo(g.x1, y);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      label(name, g.x0, y - 18, 0.45, 'left', 10, col);
    }
    const holes = 1 - fill1;
    const full = holes < 1e-6;
    label(
      full
        ? 'full: nobody has anywhere to go'
        : holes < 0.01
          ? 'nearly full, but its holes can move'
          : 'partly filled: the sea can lean',
      g.x1,
      g.y1 - 18,
      0.45,
      'right',
      10,
      full ? WARM : GREEN
    );

    for (const m of movers) {
      const y = (m.band === 1 ? g.y0 : g.y1) + Math.sin(clock * 2 + m.ph) * 2.4;
      ctx.fillStyle = m.band === 1 ? UPPER : LOWER;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(g.x0 + m.x * wpx, y, 4.2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    }
    for (const j of jumps) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(245,158,11,${Math.max(0, j.life) * 0.8})`;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;
      arrow(j.x, j.y0, j.x, j.y1, 5);
    }

    // which way, and how fast
    const vpx = Math.max(-90, Math.min(90, vDrift / 12000));
    ctx.strokeStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.fillStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    if (Math.abs(vpx) > 2) {
      const cx = CRYS.x + CRYS.w / 2;
      arrow(cx - vpx / 2, CRYS.y + 70, cx + vpx / 2, CRYS.y + 70, 7);
    }
    label(
      Math.abs(vDrift) < 1 ? 'no net motion' : `drift ${(vDrift / 1000).toFixed(1)} km/s`,
      CRYS.x + CRYS.w / 2,
      CRYS.y + 52,
      0.8,
      'center',
      13,
      Math.abs(vDrift) < 1 ? inkA(0.6) : GREEN
    );
    label(`${nAtoms} atoms at a = ${state.a.toFixed(2)} Å`, CRYS.x + 14, CRYS.y + 26, 0.5, 'left', 11);
  }

  // --- E(k) and the occupied sea ---------------------------------------------

  function drawBands() {
    panel(BANDS, 'ALLOWED ENERGIES  E(k), AND WHO SITS WHERE');
    const px = BANDS.x + 52, py = BANDS.y + 30, pw = BANDS.w - 76, ph = BANDS.h - 84;
    const eLo = Math.min(band1(0), band1(Math.PI)) - 0.7;
    const eHi = Math.max(band2(0), band2(Math.PI)) + 0.7;
    const X = (th: number) => px + ((th + Math.PI) / (2 * Math.PI)) * pw;
    const Y = (e: number) => py + ph - ((e - eLo) / (eHi - eLo)) * ph;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.2);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();

    if (gap() > 0.02) {
      ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(245,158,11,0.07)';
      ctx.fillRect(px, Y(EP - 2 * tP()), pw, Y(ES + 2 * tS()) - Y(EP - 2 * tP()));
      label(`gap ${gap().toFixed(2)} eV`, px + pw - 6, (Y(EP - 2 * tP()) + Y(ES + 2 * tS())) / 2 + 4, 0.6, 'right', 11, WARM);
    }

    // the bands themselves
    for (const [fn, col] of [[band1, LOWER], [band2, UPPER]] as [(t: number) => number, string][]) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = col;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let i = 0; i <= 120; i++) {
        const th = -Math.PI + (2 * Math.PI * i) / 120;
        i ? ctx.lineTo(X(th), Y(fn(th))) : ctx.moveTo(X(th), Y(fn(th)));
      }
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    // every occupied state, as a dot whose weight is its occupancy
    for (let i = 0; i < NK; i += 3) {
      const th = thetas[i];
      for (const [occ, fn, col] of [
        [occ1[i] ?? 0, band1, LOWER],
        [occ2[i] ?? 0, band2, UPPER],
      ] as [number, (t: number) => number, string][]) {
        if (occ < 0.02) continue;
        ctx.globalAlpha = Math.min(1, occ);
        ctx.fillStyle = col;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(X(th), Y(fn(th)), 3.4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
        ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      }
    }

    // Fermi level
    ctx.strokeStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.setLineDash([5, 4]);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, Y(EF));
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, Y(EF));
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    label(`E_F ${EF.toFixed(2)} eV`, px + 4, Y(EF) - 6, 0.85, 'left', 11, GREEN);

    // how far the sea has leaned
    if (Math.abs(shift) > 0.02) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = ACC;
      ctx.fillStyle = ACC;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;
      const y = py + 12;
      arrow(X(0) - (shift > 0 ? 0 : 40), y, X(0) + (shift > 0 ? 40 : -40), y, 6);
      label('the sea leans', X(0) + (shift > 0 ? 48 : -48), y + 4, 0.6, shift > 0 ? 'left' : 'right', 10, ACC);
    }

    label('−π/a', px, py + ph + 18, 0.4, 'left', 10);
    label('0', X(0), py + ph + 18, 0.4, 'center', 10);
    label('+π/a', px + pw, py + ph + 18, 0.4, 'right', 10);
    label('wavenumber k', px + pw / 2, py + ph + 34, 0.4, 'center', 10);
    label(`${eHi.toFixed(1)} eV`, px - 6, py + 6, 0.4, 'right', 10);
    label(`${eLo.toFixed(1)} eV`, px - 6, py + ph, 0.4, 'right', 10);
  }

  // --- density of states and occupancy ---------------------------------------

  function drawOcc() {
    panel(OCC, 'HOW MANY STATES, AND HOW MANY ARE TAKEN');
    const px = OCC.x + 54, py = OCC.y + 30, pw = OCC.w - 150, ph = OCC.h - 118;
    const eLo = Math.min(band1(0), band1(Math.PI)) - 0.7;
    const eHi = Math.max(band2(0), band2(Math.PI)) + 0.7;
    const Y = (e: number) => py + ph - ((e - eLo) / (eHi - eLo)) * ph;

    // histogram the k grid: the pile-ups at the band edges are van Hove peaks
    const NB = 90;
    const dos = new Array(NB).fill(0);
    const bin = (e: number) => Math.floor(((e - eLo) / (eHi - eLo)) * NB);
    for (const th of thetas) {
      for (const e of [band1(th), band2(th)]) {
        const b = bin(e);
        if (b >= 0 && b < NB) dos[b]++;
      }
    }
    const dmax = Math.max(1, ...dos);

    for (let b = 0; b < NB; b++) {
      if (!dos[b]) continue;
      const e = eLo + ((b + 0.5) / NB) * (eHi - eLo);
      const y = Y(e), h = ph / NB + 1;
      const wBar = (dos[b] / dmax) * pw;
      const col = e > (ES + EP) / 2 ? UPPER : LOWER;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.2;
      ctx.fillStyle = col;
      ctx.fillRect(px, y - h / 2, wBar, h);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      // the taken share
      ctx.fillStyle = col;
      ctx.fillRect(px, y - h / 2, wBar * fermi(e, EF), h);
    }

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.2);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();

    // Fermi-Dirac, drawn against its own axis on the right
    const fx = px + pw + 26, fw = 62;
    ctx.strokeStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let i = 0; i <= 120; i++) {
      const e = eLo + ((eHi - eLo) * i) / 120;
      const x = fx + fermi(e, EF) * fw;
      i ? ctx.lineTo(x, Y(e)) : ctx.moveTo(x, Y(e));
    }
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(fx, py);
    ctx.lineTo(fx, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    label('f(E)', fx + fw / 2, py + ph + 18, 0.4, 'center', 10, GREEN);
    label('1', fx + fw, py + ph + 18, 0.35, 'center', 9);
    label('0', fx, py + ph + 18, 0.35, 'center', 9);

    ctx.strokeStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.setLineDash([5, 4]);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.3;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, Y(EF));
    ctx.lineTo(fx + fw, Y(EF));
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    label('E_F', px - 6, Y(EF) + 4, 0.85, 'right', 11, GREEN);

    label('density of states', px, py + ph + 18, 0.4, 'left', 10);
    label(`kT = ${(kT() * 1000).toFixed(1)} meV`, px, py - 10, 0.5, 'left', 11, WARM);
    label(verdict(), OCC.x + OCC.w / 2, OCC.y + OCC.h - 34, 0.9, 'center', 15, verdictColour());
    label(
      carriers > 1e-12
        ? `free carriers: ${carriers.toExponential(1)} per state`
        : 'free carriers: none worth counting',
      OCC.x + OCC.w / 2,
      OCC.y + OCC.h - 14,
      0.45,
      'center',
      11
    );
  }

  function verdictColour() {
    const v = verdict();
    return v.startsWith('metal') ? GREEN : v === 'semiconductor' ? WARM : LOWER;
  }

  // --- readouts --------------------------------------------------------------

  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const setRow = (n: number, lab: string, val: string) => {
    el('l' + n).innerHTML = subHtml(lab);
    el('r' + n).textContent = val;
  };
  const setEq = equationBar();
  function updateReadout() {
    setRow(1, 'Verdict', verdict());
    setRow(2, 'Band gap E_g', gap() > 0.02 ? gap().toFixed(3) + ' eV' : 'none, they overlap');
    setRow(3, 'Lower band width', (4 * tS()).toFixed(3) + ' eV');
    setRow(4, 'Fermi level E_F', EF.toFixed(3) + ' eV');
    setRow(5, 'Free carriers', carriers > 1e-12 ? carriers.toExponential(2) : '< 1e-12');
    setRow(6, 'Drift velocity', Math.abs(vDrift) < 1 ? '0 m/s' : (vDrift / 1000).toFixed(2) + ' km/s');
    setRow(7, 'Thermal energy kT', (kT() * 1000).toFixed(2) + ' meV');
    setEq([
      [
        ['E_g', WARM],
        '\\text{ against }',
        ['k_BT', GREEN],
        ':\\quad n \\propto e^{-E_g/2k_BT}',
      ],
      [
        [`E_g = ${gap() > 0.02 ? gap().toFixed(3) + '\\,\\text{eV}' : '0'}`, WARM],
        [`\\quad k_BT = ${(kT() * 1000).toFixed(2)}\\,\\text{meV}`, GREEN],
        `\\quad 4t = ${(4 * tS()).toFixed(3)}\\,\\text{eV}`,
        `\\quad E_F = ${EF.toFixed(3)}\\,\\text{eV}`,
      ],
      [
        'a gap only means anything next to kT: small is a semiconductor, large is an insulator',
      ],
    ]);
  }

  // --- loop ------------------------------------------------------------------

  let clock = 0;
  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    label('Band Theory', 20, 30, 0.85, 'left', 14);
    label(
      `${state.n} electron${state.n === 1 ? '' : 's'} per atom · ${verdict()}`,
      20,
      52,
      0.55,
      'left',
      11,
      verdictColour()
    );
    const legend: [string, string][] = [
      [LOWER, 'lower band'],
      [UPPER, 'upper band'],
      [GREEN, 'Fermi level'],
    ];
    let x = W - 20;
    for (let k = legend.length - 1; k >= 0; k--) {
      const [c, tx] = legend[k];
      const tw = textWidth(tx, 11);
      label(tx, x, 30, 0.55, 'right', 11);
      ctx.fillStyle = c;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x - tw - 11, 26, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      x -= tw + 30;
    }
    drawSplit();
    drawCrystal();
    drawBands();
    drawOcc();
  }

  let last = performance.now();
  function frame(now: number) {
    let dt = (now - last) / 1000;
    last = now;
    dt = Math.min(0.05, Math.max(0, dt)) * state.rate;
    if (state.running) {
      clock += dt;
      // the sea leans until scattering balances the push
      shift += ((state.field * 0.55 - shift) * 4) * dt;
      stepCrystal(dt);
    }
    recompute();
    draw();
    updateReadout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // --- controls --------------------------------------------------------------

  const runBtn = el('run');
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', () => {
    buildMovers();
    jumps = [];
    shift = 0;
  });

  let ready = false;
  function bindRange(id: string, apply: (n: number) => void) {
    const inp = el(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    const run = () => apply(+inp.value);
    inp.addEventListener('input', run);
    run();
  }
  bindRange('a', (n) => {
    state.a = n / 100;
    el('aval').textContent = `${state.a.toFixed(2)} Å`;
  });
  bindRange('n', (n) => {
    state.n = n;
    el('nval').textContent = String(n);
    if (ready) buildMovers();
  });
  bindRange('temp', (n) => {
    state.temp = n;
    el('tval').textContent = `${n} K`;
  });
  bindRange('field', (n) => {
    state.field = n / 100;
    el('fval').textContent = state.field.toFixed(2);
  });
  bindRange('rate', (n) => {
    state.rate = n / 100;
    el('rateval').textContent = `${state.rate.toFixed(1)}×`;
  });
  (el('levels') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.levels = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked;
  });

  buildMovers();
  recompute();
  ready = true;
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

<style>
  .bt-canvas {
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .scale-hint {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-top: 3px;
  }
  .check {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .check input {
    accent-color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
